I lost game 19: I played Black against the 14k opponent and resigned at move 67, about 30 points behind. My record as Black is now 0 wins, 9 losses and 1 draw.

- **Opening:** C3 and G4 left a gap at the bottom. White wedged in at E4, then D4 and D3 built a wall on row 4. The stone at D3 sat inside my bottom area.
- **Right-side invasion:** My H7 invasion was too small to make two eyes and died.
- **Near-disaster:** At move 53 my 14-stone left group had been squeezed down to one liberty (E5) without my noticing. The liberty-counter script (`libs.py`) caught it, and I saved the group with A3 and B2. Those moves also captured 2 stones, and I captured 3 more with B8 and A8 afterwards.
- **Decisive loss:** White used D3 as an anchor and invaded my bottom with C2, D1, E2, F2 and G1. My bottom-right group (9 stones) was a wall on row 3 with no eye space and died. I spent the moves that could have made it an eye capturing those 3 stones on the left.

I updated `CLAUDE.md` with:
- the full move record and analysis of this game;
- a new top lesson: count each group's real eyes, not just its liberties, and defend first when a group has no eyes and enemy stones are touching its area;
- a reminder to run `libs.py` every move once groups are in contact;
- the plan for next time: as Black, drop to 16k and open with C3 then C7 so nothing fits between them; as White, stay at 12k.
